    "scenario": "MPLS TE Autoroute Announce and Tunnel Metric",
    "goals": "• OSPF area 0, addressing, Loopback0 interfaces, an MPLS core with LDP and the MPLS traffic engineering baseline are already configured.\n• {{router1_name}} already has the TE tunnel Tunnel{{tunnel_id}} towards {{router4_name}} Loopback0 ({{router4_loopback0_ip}}), pinned through {{router2_name}} by the explicit path {{explicit_path_name}}, and the tunnel is up.\n• The links that {{router2_name}} and {{router3_name}} use towards {{router4_name}} already carry a high OSPF cost, and the tunnel carries no traffic yet, because OSPF still computes its shortest path over the physical interfaces. Make {{router1_name}} install the tunnel as the path for the destinations that sit behind the tunnel tail, so that its routing table reaches {{router4_loopback0_cidr}} through Tunnel{{tunnel_id}}.\n• Give the tunnel a fixed cost of {{tunnel_metric}} that does not follow the cost of the underlying physical path, so that the tunnel wins over the expensive physical path.\n• Do not add a static route, do not change any interface OSPF cost, and do not change the path the tunnel takes: {{router2_name}} must still be the transit router.",
